# Saga X Ventures — environment template
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill it in. .env.local is gitignored and
# must stay that way: it holds live keys. This template holds none.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Nothing here is needed to run the public pages. The site builds and serves
# the homepage, coaching, Mastery Signal, blog, about, contact and privacy
# with every value below left blank. They are needed for the parts that store
# or send something: enquiries, events, email and payment.
#
# When you put these into Vercel later, add them under the Production
# environment. Anything starting NEXT_PUBLIC_ is visible in the browser;
# everything else must not be.


# ─── Site ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used to build absolute URLs for payment callbacks and email links.
# Locally this is http://localhost:3000. In production it is the live domain.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000


# ─── Supabase ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create a NEW project for this site. Do not reuse the signal platform's
# shared project: it holds member and billing data, and a mistake in a public
# marketing site should not be able to reach it.
#
# Where: supabase.com → your project → Project Settings → API
#
# URL and the publishable (anon) key are safe in the browser. The service role
# key is NOT — it bypasses row level security entirely. It must never be
# prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_, never imported into a client component, and never
# pasted into a chat or a log.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=


# ─── Admin access ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The single email address allowed to sign in to /admin, and the address the
# owner's own order notifications are sent to. Sign-in is a magic link, so
# there is no password to leak. Any other address is refused even if it has a
# valid Supabase account.
#
# It is here rather than in `site.ts` on purpose: it is the owner's working
# inbox, not a published contact address, and the repo is not where a private
# address belongs.
ADMIN_EMAIL=


# ─── Resend (email) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where: resend.com → API Keys
#
# RESEND_FROM must be on a domain you have verified in Resend, which means
# adding its DNS records in Cloudflare first. Sending from an unverified
# domain silently lands in spam.
#
# RESEND_REPLY_TO is where a member's reply actually goes. Set it to the
# address you read, not to the no-reply sender.
RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_FROM="Saga X Ventures <no-reply@sagaxventures.com>"
RESEND_REPLY_TO=enquiry@sagaxventures.com


# ─── Billplz (payment) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SANDBOX AND LIVE ARE SEPARATE ACCOUNTS, on different domains, with
# different dashboards, keys, collections and signing keys.
#
#   Sandbox:  www.billplz-sandbox.com   — sign up separately, it is free
#   Live:     www.billplz.com
#
# Both sets live here at once so neither is ever pasted over the other.
# BILLPLZ_SANDBOX chooses which set is read:
#
#   BILLPLZ_SANDBOX=true   →  the BILLPLZ_SANDBOX_* values below
#   BILLPLZ_SANDBOX=false  →  the BILLPLZ_LIVE_* values below
#
# Switching is one word. Nothing else has to move.
#
# Where to find each, in whichever dashboard matches:
#   ..._API_KEY        Settings → Account Settings → API keys ("Secret Key")
#   ..._COLLECTION_ID  Billing → Collections → open one → the id in its URL
#   ..._X_SIGNATURE    Settings → Account Settings → X Signature Key
#
# The X Signature key verifies that a callback really came from Billplz.
# Without it, anyone who learns the callback URL can mark an order paid. It
# is not optional.
#
# Leave BILLPLZ_SANDBOX=true until a real payment has been tested end to end.
# Sandbox credentials are refused outright on the live domain, so they cannot
# be served to a real buyer by accident.
BILLPLZ_SANDBOX=true

BILLPLZ_SANDBOX_API_KEY=
BILLPLZ_SANDBOX_COLLECTION_ID=
BILLPLZ_SANDBOX_X_SIGNATURE=

BILLPLZ_LIVE_API_KEY=
BILLPLZ_LIVE_COLLECTION_ID=
BILLPLZ_LIVE_X_SIGNATURE=

# The three names below are what this file used before the split. They are
# read only when BILLPLZ_SANDBOX=false and the BILLPLZ_LIVE_* ones are empty,
# so anything already pasted here keeps working. There is no fallback in the
# sandbox direction: a live key sent to the sandbox host is rejected exactly
# like a wrong one, and that is the confusion the split exists to end.
BILLPLZ_API_KEY=
BILLPLZ_COLLECTION_ID=
BILLPLZ_X_SIGNATURE=


# ─── Telegram (order notifications) ──────────────────────────────────────
# The bot that tells the owner a package has been paid for: who bought it,
# which one, and how to reach them.
#
# Token: message @BotFather → /newbot (or /token for an existing bot).
# Chat id: message your bot once, then open
#   https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates
# and read message.chat.id from the response.
#
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID is where the message goes, and nowhere else. It carries a
# buyer's name, email and phone, so a wrong id leaks a customer's details to
# a stranger's chat.
#
# NOTE: the receipt upload and the inline Approve button described in §7.13
# of the design are NOT part of the first release — the owner chose Billplz
# only, so there is no receipt to approve. If that button is ever added, the
# handler must accept callbacks from this chat id and no other: it releases a
# paid registration link, and an unprotected inline button is a public
# endpoint.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=


# ─── Account record (/copytrade chart) ───────────────────────────────────
# The reporter EA on the VPS posts the master account's balance, equity and
# deals to /api/record/ingest. See mt5/README.md.
#
# RECORD_INGEST_SECRET is what lets a request write figures the public page
# shows as the record. 32+ random characters (openssl rand -hex 32), the same
# value as the EA's InpSecret input, and nowhere else.
#
# RECORD_ACCOUNT_LOGIN is the master account's MT5 login. Reports from any
# other account are refused, so a follower's figures can never be published.
#
# Both blank: the chart shows its empty state and the endpoint answers 503.
RECORD_INGEST_SECRET=
RECORD_ACCOUNT_LOGIN=

# More accounts running Fuky AA, shown as tabs beside the master. Each needs
# its own reporter EA on its own terminal (same secret). UNIT is required —
# `cent` or `usd` — and an account without a valid one is not shown at all:
# a cent account read as dollars would show a balance 100x too large.
# RECORD_ACCOUNT_UNIT may override the master's default of cent.
RECORD_ACCOUNT_LOGIN_2=
RECORD_ACCOUNT_UNIT_2=
RECORD_ACCOUNT_LOGIN_3=
RECORD_ACCOUNT_UNIT_3=


# ─── Mastery Terminal (news wire) ────────────────────────────────────────
# See docs/terminal.md.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY pays for classifying headlines. From Claude Console →
# API keys. Keep the Console's monthly spend limit set: a run is capped at 75
# headlines, but the limit is what stops a bug from spending the credit.
#
# CRON_SECRET is what the scheduler sends as `Authorization: Bearer ...` to
# /api/terminal/ingest (and /api/reminders). 32+ random characters.
#
# TERMINAL_INGEST_SECRET, when set, replaces CRON_SECRET for the ingest route
# only. Use it when something other than Vercel's scheduler calls the route
# (Supabase pg_cron on the Hobby plan), so that caller cannot also trigger
# /api/reminders.
#
# TERMINAL_FEED_KEY is what Mastery Signal's server sends to
# /api/terminal/feed. Its own random value, not the cron secret: Mastery can
# read the wire, it cannot make it spend.
#
# FINNHUB_API_KEY is optional. Without it the wire uses GDELT and the Fed only.
# TERMINAL_MODEL is optional and defaults to claude-haiku-5-5.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
CRON_SECRET=
TERMINAL_INGEST_SECRET=
TERMINAL_FEED_KEY=
FINNHUB_API_KEY=
TERMINAL_MODEL=

# UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY (optional) adds a photo to medium and high stories.
# unsplash.com/developers -> New Application -> Access Key. Free tier allows
# 50 searches an hour; the wire uses at most 4 a run.
UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=

# BLS_API_KEY (optional) for Macro data. bls.gov/developers, free. Without it
# the BLS v1 API still works: 25 requests a day, ten years each.
BLS_API_KEY=


# ─── 21st.dev (build time only) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed to run `npx shadcn@latest add` against a 21st.dev registry
# component. Not used at runtime, not needed in Vercel.
# Where: 21st.dev/mcp
API_KEY_21ST=
